Z||000032||OcalaFiero||12-26-2001||11:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>Part of my Christmas came last week- a trip to the doctor with my healthy wife and saw some sonogram (sp?) images of our yet to be born son. The real fun starts in about 4 months   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Oh, and some new school clothes, a few houses for the train set and a new pair of shoes.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>After going through my baby girl's delivery last Friday, I can say that, without a doubt, nothing compares to the birth of a child, it puts everything in perspective...and gives you a chance to catch up on late night PFF reading. Best of luck, you guys are in the home stretch.<P>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<P>||||reg||1
Z||000033||Elvira||12-26-2001||04:33 PM||||After going through my baby girl's delivery last Friday, I can say that, without a doubt, nothing compares to the birth of a child, <P>Except the birth of a second one!  Beautiful little girl and great choice on a name, especially the middle name(that's my real name!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Chester and I are at the end of the home stretch.  Our daughter is 18 1/2 and graduated last June.  Our son is 17 1/2 and almost there schoolwise!  Christmas is definately fun with teens!  Chester and I buy for each other throughout the year so Christmas day is for the kids!  I got my blue GT and the motor to go in it and Chester got his Mr. Mikes seats coming along with a closet of gadgets to go in his GT and we got more tools as "our" present.  Can NEVER have too many tools!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles<BR>84 Indy<BR>87 4-seater||||reg||1
